        "badgeTag": "ALUMNUS"
      },
      "timeAgo": "1h ago",
      "endorsedBy": "Endorsed by 4 other Alumni from Razorpay & Atlassian",
      "steps": [
        {
          "headline": "1. First 2 Months (LLD & Clean Code)",
          "content": "Master SOLID principles and the 5 foundational Design Patterns (Factory, Strategy, Observer, Decorator, State). Don't just skim theory—code complete command-line projects for Splitwise and an Elevator System."
        },
        {
          "headline": "2. Months 3-4 (Concurrency & DB Modeling)",
          "content": "Learn B-Tree database indexing, ACID transaction isolation levels, and caching strategies (Redis TTL patterns). In interviews, thread-safety is where candidates get filtered."
        },
        {
          "headline": "3. Months 5-6 (System Integration & Bottlenecks)",
          "content": "Deploy your Spring/Django REST APIs with Docker. Use JMeter or Locust to generate 500 req/sec to witness database locking in real time."
        }
      ],
      "proTip": "Tier-1 interviewers care about clean interfaces, unit testing, and design extensibility way more than distributed consensus algorithms like Raft or Paxos!",
      "codeSnippet": {
        "fileName": "PaymentStrategy.java",
        "language": "java",
        "code": "// Key pattern: Strategy Pattern for Payment Gateway\npublic interface PaymentStrategy {\n    TransactionResult pay(BigDecimal amount, PaymentContext ctx);\n}\n\npublic class UpiPaymentStrategy implements PaymentStrategy {\n    @Override\n    public TransactionResult pay(BigDecimal amount, PaymentContext ctx) {\n        // Idempotent VPA handle routing\n        return npciClient.initiateTransfer(ctx.getVpa(), amount);\n    }\n}"
      },
